  "final_message": "The bug was that `add_tag` used `tags=[]` as its default. Python creates that list only once, so every call that left out `tags` added to the same shared list.\n\nI changed the default to `tags=None` and create a fresh `[]` inside the function when it's `None`. If the caller passes a `tags` list, the function still appends to that list directly. `remove_tag` is unchanged, and `test_public.py` now passes (1 test).\n\nDONE: Replaced the mutable default `tags=[]` in `add_tag` with `None` plus a fresh list per call; `test_public.py` passes.",
